From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quill <siinspam@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:14:31 +0000
Subject: feat(nako): native tool calling for antigravity-oauth

A request with tools used to go to agy as text: tool schemas pasted into the
prompt, calls written back as <tool_call> JSON, and the whole conversation
rebuilt as one capped text blob whenever a request did not strictly extend the
last one. In long sessions that fed on itself: malformed call JSON made the host
retry, each retry threw the agy session away, the rebuild cut every tool result
but the newest eight to 300 characters, and the model re-read everything in huge
steps, sometimes inventing the results.

agy now keeps the conversation and calls the host's tools as real functions,
the way an ACP editor client drives it. The plugin serves the tools from a
local MCP server, hands each call to the host, and answers it when the host
sends the result. Built-in agy tools stay refused. A conversation that changed
some other way is sent once to a new session, oldest entries shortened first.
A request also fails after five minutes of silence instead of thirty.

ANTIGRAVITY_NATIVE_TOOLS=0 keeps the text bridge.

Co-authored-by: Nako <nako@quill.moe>

